<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Hindi (hi) localisation — first cut, v0.30.3.

    Same translation principles as values-ta/strings.xml:

      * Brand names ("Transfer Rate", provider names like Wise, LuLu,
        Aspora) are NOT translated — trademarks; recognised in their
        English forms even in Hindi-speaking contexts.
      * Currency codes (AED, INR, ₹) stay as-is.
      * "BEST" / "MANUAL" badges stay English (translatable=false at
        the source).
      * Toolbar chips (AUTO/LIGHT/DARK/REFRESH) stay English for
        compactness — icons + position make them self-evident.
      * Body text and headings ARE translated, with one rule:
        finance / technical terms commonly transliterated by NRIs in
        spoken Hindi get transliterated rather than fully Hindi-ised,
        e.g. "mid-market" → "मिड-मार्केट" rather than the literal
        "मध्य-बाज़ार" which would feel academic.

    Native-speaker review pending — please flag any phrases that read
    awkward.  Encoding is UTF-8; Devanagari renders via Android's
    bundled Noto Sans Devanagari fallback.
-->
